where are your other friends?

267
00:12:46,750 --> 00:12:49,840
You told me to prepare
so many guest rooms.

268
00:12:50,870 --> 00:12:53,320
They're probably out
looking for places to visit, Mom.

269
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:55,060
They'll likely be back by this evening.

270
00:13:01,930 --> 00:13:03,970
Mom, this is P'Three,

271
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,210
the one I told you about.

272
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:06,250
Hel... Oh...

273
00:13:07,690 --> 00:13:08,480
Hello.

274
00:13:09,730 --> 00:13:10,580
I see.

275
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:14,940
The one who recruited you
for the Pro League team?

276
00:13:16,780 --> 00:13:17,550
That's right.

277
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:27,500
P'Three,

278
00:13:27,590 --> 00:13:30,560
this is Oom, my friend.

279
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:32,070
She's my best friend from school.

280
00:13:32,110 --> 00:13:33,150
Oh, a best friend.

281
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:35,570
More than just a best friend.

282
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:38,870
Oom understands Soh better than anyone.

283
00:13:39,110 --> 00:13:40,990
Where there's Oom, there's Soh.

284
00:13:42,670 --> 00:13:45,120
Where there's Soh, there's Oom.

285
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:52,090
These two were joined at the hip.

286
00:13:52,310 --> 00:13:55,980
I even thought they were dating.

287
00:13:56,860 --> 00:13:58,720
Mom, what are you even saying?

288
00:14:09,890 --> 00:14:10,810
Wow.

289
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,590
I didn't know sai oua
could smell this amazing.

290
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:14,530
Look at this sticky rice.
It's perfectly steamed.

291
00:14:14,910 --> 00:14:18,250
- Your cooking is incredible, Mom.
- Oom actually made it.

292
00:14:29,610 --> 00:14:30,980
Soh, have some of this.

293
00:14:31,390 --> 00:14:32,600
Give me your plate.
I'll get some for you.

294
00:14:32,620 --> 00:14:35,000
It must be hard
to find food like this in Bangkok.

295
00:14:35,860 --> 00:14:37,570
- Here, eat up.
- Thanks.

296
00:14:38,110 --> 00:14:39,590
This one, too.

297
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:41,140
- Thanks, Oom.
- Take this one, too.

298
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:44,010
Soh, try some nam prik ong.

299
00:14:44,150 --> 00:14:46,010
I know you like spicy food. Here.

300
00:14:48,630 --> 00:14:50,040
Soh doesn't like tomatoes.

301
00:15:17,170 --> 00:15:19,980
P'Three, make sure you eat a lot.

302
00:15:23,910 --> 00:15:26,500
Here, Oom. You should eat up as well.

303
00:15:26,530 --> 00:15:28,560
You're too busy serving everyone.

304
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:30,380
You're so tiny yourself.

305
00:15:30,530 --> 00:15:31,650
Thanks, Mom.

306
00:15:32,310 --> 00:15:35,320
Oh, tomorrow is
your wedding anniversary, isn't it?

307
00:15:36,350 --> 00:15:37,140
Yes, it is.

308
00:15:37,220 --> 00:15:41,050
I'm planning to go donate things
up on the mountain, like every year.

309
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:43,140
What a shame. I'm busy this year.

310
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:45,370
If I weren't, I would go help you
like I always do.

311
00:15:45,830 --> 00:15:46,870
It's alright, dear.

312
00:15:46,970 --> 00:15:50,460
I think I'll ask Soh's friends
to help with the heavy lifting.

313
00:15:51,580 --> 00:15:52,380
Would that be okay?

314
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:53,480
Oh...

315
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:01,790
Absolutely, Mom.

316
00:16:01,930 --> 00:16:02,720
When it comes to...

317
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:05,850
anything involving manual labor,
I'm your man.

318
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:06,930
I've never been outmatched.

319
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:12,490
Then this auntie
will be counting on you.

320
00:16:16,870 --> 00:16:18,260
Alright.

321
00:16:22,870 --> 00:16:24,840
- Oom, let's eat.
- Go ahead, Mom.

322
00:16:24,860 --> 00:16:25,620
Here.

323
00:16:26,040 --> 00:16:29,390
Eat up. Let me get this for you.

324
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:32,420
I really put my heart into this dish.

325
00:16:32,550 --> 00:16:33,720
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

326
00:16:35,050 --> 00:16:36,750
- Have as much as you'd like.
- Thank you.

327
00:16:36,780 --> 00:16:37,690
Let me serve you.

328
00:16:37,750 --> 00:16:39,350
Serve some for Soh, too.

329
00:16:39,530 --> 00:16:40,470
Oh, he's fine.

330
00:16:48,730 --> 00:16:50,390
I'm so full, Soh.

331
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:52,900
Like, I'm stuffed.

332
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:56,800
I didn't think
you'd finish everything like that.

333
00:16:57,110 --> 00:16:59,660
My mom made quite a lot

334
00:16:59,690 --> 00:17:01,840
since she was planning to
give some to others, too.

335
00:17:01,860 --> 00:17:03,730
Oh, don't worry about that.

336
00:17:03,820 --> 00:17:05,810
To win her heart
and become her favorite son-in-law,

337
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:07,870
I could eat even more than this.

338
00:17:07,890 --> 00:17:09,630
If your mom makes more,
I'll keep eating.

339
00:17:13,930 --> 00:17:14,660
But...

340
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:18,760
no matter how I try
to win your mom's heart,

341
00:17:19,130 --> 00:17:21,330
she's still going to prefer Oom anyway.

342
00:17:21,690 --> 00:17:23,680
She likes Oom more than me.

343
00:17:23,970 --> 00:17:26,830
If she tries to block me

344
00:17:27,510 --> 00:17:29,320
and pushes you two to date,

345
00:17:30,180 --> 00:17:32,110
where does that leave me, Soh?

346
00:17:36,650 --> 00:17:41,720
But I like you, P'Three.

347
00:17:46,950 --> 00:17:49,480
That's already a win.
You don't even have to compete.

348
00:17:52,300 --> 00:17:57,090
Besides, as for me and Oom,

349
00:17:57,540 --> 00:17:59,140
it's absolutely impossible

350
00:17:59,430 --> 00:18:02,760
because the person
Oom actually likes is...

351
00:18:03,050 --> 00:18:03,820
you.

352
00:18:05,300 --> 00:18:05,930
What?

353
00:18:06,230 --> 00:18:07,370
Me?

354
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:08,880
You mean me?

355
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:11,440
Your cooking is incredible, Mom.

356
00:18:15,790 --> 00:18:18,510
Well, when I was seeing her out,

357
00:18:18,610 --> 00:18:19,900
we chatted for a bit,

358
00:18:20,150 --> 00:18:24,470
and I found out that she's been
a fan of yours for quite some time.

359
00:18:24,500 --> 00:18:25,650
I see.

360
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:28,150
And the reason
she was acting so indifferent...

361
00:18:28,850 --> 00:18:31,620
is actually because she was just shy.

362
00:18:34,150 --> 00:18:35,300
But it's not that surprising.

363
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:37,970
If I got to meet my favorite gamer,

364
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:40,000
I probably wouldn't know
how to act, either.

365
00:18:41,220 --> 00:18:44,240
Is your favorite gamer me?

366
00:18:45,030 --> 00:18:45,610
Well...

367
00:18:46,640 --> 00:18:48,000
it has to be you, obviously.

368
00:18:49,660 --> 00:18:52,720
You feel better now, right?

369
00:18:54,890 --> 00:18:55,660
Not quite.

370
00:18:55,860 --> 00:18:56,440
Oh...

371
00:18:57,990 --> 00:19:00,880
If you could just tell me
you like me one more time,

372
00:19:00,900 --> 00:19:02,780
I'd definitely have sweet dreams
until morning.

373
00:19:03,170 --> 00:19:05,870
I wasn't really ready
when you said it just now.

374
00:19:05,900 --> 00:19:07,660
Come on, just one more time. Please...

375
00:19:12,190 --> 00:19:12,800
Oh?

376
00:19:12,820 --> 00:19:14,380
I think I'm getting sleepy now.

377
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:16,290
- Hey!
- Should we just head to bed?

378
00:19:16,320 --> 00:19:17,920
- Seriously?
- We have to wake up early tomorrow

379
00:19:17,930 --> 00:19:19,180
to get everything ready
for the mountain trip.

380
00:19:19,190 --> 00:19:20,040
What?

381
00:19:40,650 --> 00:19:42,680
Come on, don't cry.

382
00:19:44,450 --> 00:19:46,060
My mom is really kind.

383
00:19:46,660 --> 00:19:49,060
She's bound to like you
just as much as I do.

384
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:55,270
♪I'll find my way
into your heart one day,♪

385
00:19:55,300 --> 00:19:58,570
♪Getting a little closer every day,♪

386
00:20:00,020 --> 00:20:01,850
Goodnight, P'Three.

387
00:20:02,030 --> 00:20:02,960
Goodnight.

388
00:20:03,790 --> 00:20:10,290
♪Until your heart makes room for me♪

389
00:20:12,990 --> 00:20:15,250
I'll leave the loading to you.

390
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:16,650
I have to head off first.

391
00:20:16,830 --> 00:20:19,650
I told the village chief and the kids
I'd be there at 10 AM.

392
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:20,500
Sure thing, Auntie.

393
00:20:20,520 --> 00:20:23,430
Don't worry. I'll take care of it.
You can count on me.

394
00:20:35,420 --> 00:20:36,980
P'Laem, hurry up, will you?

395
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:39,360
What? Are you nagging me?

396
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:41,520
Jeez, it's P'Jack's fault.

397
00:20:41,630 --> 00:20:43,800
- What?
- He made me walk around the zoo twice.

398
00:20:43,830 --> 00:20:46,440
- Put it down.
- Put it down and get the next load.

399
00:20:46,470 --> 00:20:47,450
There's still plenty more.

400
00:20:49,490 --> 00:20:50,300
Go on.

401
00:20:50,770 --> 00:20:51,840
Get up there.

402
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:53,620
No.

403
00:20:54,750 --> 00:20:55,690
Go ahead.

404
00:20:56,640 --> 00:20:57,270
Do it.

405
00:20:58,900 --> 00:21:01,830
I guess your friend
doesn't like me very much.

406
00:21:02,170 --> 00:21:03,430
There's no way I could not like you.

407
00:21:03,460 --> 00:21:05,850
I went all the way to Bangkok
to watch you compete.

408
00:21:05,870 --> 00:21:07,110
I started playing Jungle because of you.

409
00:21:07,130 --> 00:21:10,100
I donated so much I was left
with barely any pocket money.

410
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:11,360
And now I know...

411
00:21:11,390 --> 00:21:14,320
what I should've done all along
was be honest with you...

412
00:21:14,350 --> 00:21:15,280
and ask for your autograph.

413
00:21:15,290 --> 00:21:16,360
Oh, of course.

414
00:21:16,370 --> 00:21:18,360
Wow, quite a long speech there.

415
00:21:18,830 --> 00:21:21,300
I've been a fan
since you were in Numb2r.

416
00:21:21,380 --> 00:21:23,400
It's a shame that whole thing happened.

417
00:21:23,630 --> 00:21:26,340
Otherwise, I'm sure
Numb2r would've gone far,

418
00:21:26,430 --> 00:21:28,480
maybe even all the way
to the international leagues.

419
00:21:28,810 --> 00:21:31,530
Maybe not.
We weren't really in sync anyway,

420
00:21:31,560 --> 00:21:33,680
and we didn't always see eye to eye.

421
00:21:35,190 --> 00:21:36,270
Thank you.

422
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:39,450
Well, I'll take my leave now.

423
00:21:39,670 --> 00:21:42,160
It's too bad I can't go with you all.

424
00:21:42,190 --> 00:21:43,940
Anyway, good luck, P'Three.

425
00:21:43,960 --> 00:21:46,040
I'm sure
you'll take first place in the APL.

426
00:21:46,140 --> 00:21:47,640
B.S. Brothers have gotta go for it!

427
00:21:47,720 --> 00:21:49,000
Definitely gotta go for it.

428
00:21:51,210 --> 00:21:52,820
- I'm off, Soh.
- Okay.

429
00:21:53,100 --> 00:21:54,860
- Come visit us often.
- Will do.

430
00:21:55,150 --> 00:21:56,180
- Bye-bye.
- Bye, P'Three.

431
00:21:56,200 --> 00:21:56,920
Okay.

432
00:22:06,350 --> 00:22:07,430
Hello, Mom?

433
00:22:09,290 --> 00:22:11,870
Oh, okay. I'll bring it over.

434
00:22:14,340 --> 00:22:15,020
Sure.

435
00:22:16,670 --> 00:22:17,460
P'Three,

436
00:22:17,630 --> 00:22:20,450
my mom told me
to bring the first-aid kit.

437
00:22:21,130 --> 00:22:21,920
I'm exhausted.

438
00:22:24,170 --> 00:22:24,920
Is it this one?

439
00:22:24,940 --> 00:22:26,500
This one with the keychain?

440
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:28,100
Yes.

441
00:22:28,410 --> 00:22:31,050
- Okay, I'll put it in the truck, then.
- Alright.

442
00:22:31,080 --> 00:22:32,170
Okay.

443
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:37,730
Oh...

444
00:22:39,140 --> 00:22:39,740
Soh?

445
00:22:40,290 --> 00:22:41,960
Soh, what's wrong?

446
00:22:42,910 --> 00:22:44,380
I don't know. I think it's a bug.

447
00:22:44,430 --> 00:22:45,640
Here, let me check.

448
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:47,490
Oh...

449
00:22:48,910 --> 00:22:50,990
There, I got it for you.

450
00:22:51,010 --> 00:22:52,190
There's more, P'Jack.

451
00:22:52,320 --> 00:22:54,710
- Is it red? Can you check?
- It's really red.

452
00:22:55,440 --> 00:22:57,040
- It's totally red.
- It's so itchy.

453
00:22:57,370 --> 00:22:59,290
I'll handle it for you.
Where is it? What's its name?

454
00:22:59,320 --> 00:23:00,780
- It already got away.
- It got away?

455
00:23:00,810 --> 00:23:01,810
- Hey.
- Yes?

456
00:23:02,510 --> 00:23:04,140
Our shifts got swapped.

457
00:23:04,290 --> 00:23:05,520
You're supposed to go to the airport.

458
00:23:05,600 --> 00:23:07,940
Oh, okay. My apologies.

459
00:23:09,540 --> 00:23:11,460
Kids, get the stuff in the truck.

460
00:23:11,770 --> 00:23:13,280
Did he say Sumatra, the island?

461
00:23:13,770 --> 00:23:15,800
- It's "sumater." It means sorry.
- Oh, I see.

462
00:23:33,920 --> 00:23:35,430
♪Pancake rolls♪

463
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:38,830
- ♪I want some pancake rolls♪
- ♪Pancake rolls♪

464
00:23:40,550 --> 00:23:41,830
- Hey, hey!
- Huh? What?

465
00:23:41,860 --> 00:23:43,330
Sir, stop the car!

466
00:23:45,180 --> 00:23:45,830
What is it?

467
00:23:46,040 --> 00:23:46,690
What the hell?

468
00:23:46,830 --> 00:23:47,860
What are you looking for?

469
00:23:48,450 --> 00:23:49,560
What are you looking for?

470
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:02,150
Soh...

471
00:24:02,290 --> 00:24:03,680
What's wrong, P'Three?

472
00:24:04,180 --> 00:24:06,600
I think I lost your mom's first-aid kit.

473
00:24:21,670 --> 00:24:22,510
What's up?

474
00:24:23,240 --> 00:24:25,240
- Long time no see, man.
- You're finally back.

475
00:24:25,380 --> 00:24:27,330
Welcome back, bro.

476
00:24:28,510 --> 00:24:30,520
What's the word?

477
00:24:30,730 --> 00:24:32,600
- It was lonely as hell without you.
- Come on.

478
00:24:33,190 --> 00:24:35,560
- I'm back, buddy.
- Yeah, I couldn't play right at all.

479
00:24:36,100 --> 00:24:37,050
Since you're back,

480
00:24:37,410 --> 00:24:38,540
I've got a ride ready for you.

481
00:24:41,370 --> 00:24:42,400
A red truck?

482
00:24:43,810 --> 00:24:45,080
Yeah, a red truck.

483
00:24:45,130 --> 00:24:45,950
What about a van?

484
00:24:46,580 --> 00:24:49,280
The van is at the hotel,
so I rented a red truck first.

485
00:24:52,440 --> 00:24:53,990
That is so extra, man.

486
00:24:55,270 --> 00:24:56,160
Let's just rent a van.

487
00:24:56,280 --> 00:24:58,550
Don't you get what "OG" means, buddy?

488
00:24:58,900 --> 00:25:00,850
When in Chiang Mai,
you take the red truck.

489
00:25:01,380 --> 00:25:02,260
By the way,

490
00:25:03,640 --> 00:25:04,590
now that you're back,

491
00:25:05,280 --> 00:25:06,480
are you ready for the APL?

492
00:25:08,590 --> 00:25:09,840
You bet I am.

493
00:25:12,010 --> 00:25:13,960
- That's dope.
- Come on, let's go.

494
00:25:13,980 --> 00:25:15,320
Let's go explore the tea plantation!

495
00:25:15,340 --> 00:25:18,480
- One, two, three, go!
- One, two, three, go!

496
00:25:18,500 --> 00:25:19,340
- Nice!
- Come on.

497
00:25:19,370 --> 00:25:20,760
- Let's go!
- Wait, wait!

498
00:25:20,780 --> 00:25:21,700
Wait, sir.

499
00:25:22,280 --> 00:25:25,080
I'm sorry.
I actually took the wrong truck.

500
00:25:25,110 --> 00:25:26,580
A customer's belongings
are still inside.

501
00:25:26,780 --> 00:25:27,780
I have to go return them.

502
00:25:28,060 --> 00:25:29,230
I really can't take you anymore.

503
00:25:30,160 --> 00:25:31,220
I'm not sure I understood his accent.

504
00:25:31,950 --> 00:25:33,450
- What?
- What?

505
00:25:33,800 --> 00:25:35,260
Sorry, I can't go anymore.

506
00:25:36,730 --> 00:25:38,100
I've already called the other driver.

507
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:38,980
Just wait a moment.

508
00:25:39,190 --> 00:25:40,190
Okay, thank you.

509
00:25:47,580 --> 00:25:48,380
Hey, wait.

510
00:25:49,620 --> 00:25:50,490
Is it this one?

511
00:25:58,790 --> 00:26:00,270
Man, it's freaking hot.

512
00:26:02,170 --> 00:26:02,830
Help.

513
00:26:04,190 --> 00:26:05,080
Help what?

514
00:26:12,610 --> 00:26:14,100
Hurry up and give me my stuff back.

515
00:26:15,950 --> 00:26:17,630
Well, why don't you try
asking me nicely?

516
00:26:18,180 --> 00:26:20,660
I went out of my way
to bring this back to you, you know.

517
00:26:21,430 --> 00:26:22,640
Maybe I won't give it back at all.

518
00:26:24,560 --> 00:26:25,340
Ten...

519
00:26:29,410 --> 00:26:30,680
I'm giving it back right now. See?

520
00:26:30,810 --> 00:26:31,900
Hurry up, Ten!

521
00:26:32,560 --> 00:26:33,720
It's very hot.

522
00:26:34,590 --> 00:26:35,840
Ugh, I'm thirsty.

523
00:26:37,130 --> 00:26:38,640
Let's head up the mountain, guys.

524
00:26:39,840 --> 00:26:41,560
We've been in the foothill for too long.

525
00:27:02,210 --> 00:27:03,220
Hello, Mom?

526
00:27:04,260 --> 00:27:06,080
Yes, we're almost there.

527
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:10,340
Whoa, there's a long line
of kids already?

528
00:27:11,110 --> 00:27:12,440
Oh, the first-aid kit?

529
00:27:12,910 --> 00:27:15,260
P'Three is taking good care of it.
Don't worry.

530
00:27:15,630 --> 00:27:16,440
Okay.

531
00:27:18,610 --> 00:27:19,700
Alright, shall we go now?

532
00:27:19,730 --> 00:27:20,940
- Yes.
- Let's go.

533
00:27:21,410 --> 00:27:23,000
Start the engine, sir. Let's go.

534
00:27:24,140 --> 00:27:25,350
Go.

535
00:27:26,810 --> 00:27:27,610
What?

536
00:27:27,640 --> 00:27:28,500
I can't go.

537
00:27:29,050 --> 00:27:30,520
Huh? Why can't you?

538
00:27:30,590 --> 00:27:31,260
The car broke down.

539
00:27:31,490 --> 00:27:32,020
What?

540
00:27:34,180 --> 00:27:35,790
Did I wear an unlucky shirt today,

541
00:27:35,820 --> 00:27:37,650
or did I get off on the wrong foot?

542
00:27:37,750 --> 00:27:38,500
What rotten luck!

543
00:27:38,530 --> 00:27:40,120
Sir, are you pulling my leg?

544
00:27:40,570 --> 00:27:41,700
No, I'm not.

545
00:27:43,290 --> 00:27:45,140
Sir, it's been an hour.

546
00:27:45,160 --> 00:27:46,840
Are you almost done?

547
00:27:46,890 --> 00:27:48,020
I've got a mission to complete, sir.

548
00:27:48,050 --> 00:27:49,940
I have to win over my boyfriend's mom!

549
00:27:50,770 --> 00:27:52,260
- Sir!
- P'Three...

550
00:27:52,860 --> 00:27:54,920
I already called my mom
to tell her about the breakdown.

551
00:27:55,550 --> 00:27:56,780
She understands perfectly.

552
00:27:56,950 --> 00:27:58,620
You don't need to worry at all.

553
00:27:58,800 --> 00:28:00,420
Soh, thank you so much,

554
00:28:00,450 --> 00:28:02,440
but I don't want your mom
to be kept waiting.

555
00:28:03,100 --> 00:28:05,540
Sir, has the mechanic arrived yet?

556
00:28:06,420 --> 00:28:08,340
Not yet. It'll be a while.

557
00:28:09,040 --> 00:28:11,020
Could you call and tell them to hurry?

558
00:28:12,020 --> 00:28:13,500
Oh, sure.

559
00:28:13,720 --> 00:28:14,480
Thank you.

560
00:28:17,050 --> 00:28:17,740
Three,

561
00:28:18,820 --> 00:28:20,060
should I call Ten?

562
00:28:22,480 --> 00:28:23,220
Man,

563
00:28:23,990 --> 00:28:25,310
I doubt he'd even show up.

564
00:28:25,610 --> 00:28:28,160
Didn't you see
how happy they were earlier,

565
00:28:28,180 --> 00:28:29,720
seeing us all messy?

566
00:28:36,440 --> 00:28:37,080
Wait...

567
00:28:45,560 --> 00:28:46,960
Waiting for me, weren't you?

568
00:28:49,800 --> 00:28:51,340
Get in, or I might change my mind.

569
00:28:53,660 --> 00:28:54,490
Are you coming or not?

570
00:29:00,830 --> 00:29:01,650
I already knew.

571
00:29:03,010 --> 00:29:03,730
Knew what?

572
00:29:04,900 --> 00:29:06,200
That you'd show up anyway.

573
00:29:13,700 --> 00:29:14,800
They're here!

574
00:29:14,820 --> 00:29:15,840
- They're here.
- We finally made it.

575
00:29:16,500 --> 00:29:17,100
Here we are.

576
00:29:17,130 --> 00:29:19,070
- We're here?
- What is this place?

577
00:29:19,320 --> 00:29:21,520
And are those kids? Look, kids!

578
00:29:25,450 --> 00:29:27,790
Come here, kids! Your Laem is here.

579
00:29:27,820 --> 00:29:30,240
Let's dance! Six seven...

580
00:29:30,270 --> 00:29:32,270
Six seven!

581
00:29:33,570 --> 00:29:34,690
- Six seven!
- Want to take some photos?

582
00:29:34,720 --> 00:29:36,560
Photos! Come on, let's take some photos.

583
00:29:38,360 --> 00:29:39,800
Here's the kit, ma'am.

584
00:29:43,160 --> 00:29:46,840
But where is the hill tribe keychain?

585
00:29:54,690 --> 00:29:57,400
That's very important to me, son.

586
00:29:59,290 --> 00:30:01,100
It can't even be replaced.

587
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:11,070
But, I...

588
00:30:11,680 --> 00:30:12,740
I'm so sorry.

589
00:30:14,490 --> 00:30:16,920
I'll find it
and return it to you, ma'am.

590
00:30:20,280 --> 00:30:22,620
It was a wedding anniversary gift

591
00:30:22,750 --> 00:30:25,240
that my husband left for me.

592
00:30:25,450 --> 00:30:29,400
No matter what I replace it with,
it won't be the same.

593
00:30:33,260 --> 00:30:34,300
I'm so sorry.

594
00:30:35,330 --> 00:30:37,680
You trusted me to take care of it.

595
00:30:38,020 --> 00:30:40,120
You must be
really disappointed in me, right?

596
00:30:47,440 --> 00:30:49,620
Hey, it's alright.

597
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:53,420
Let's go donate the things.

598
00:30:53,460 --> 00:30:55,200
The kids have been waiting long enough.

599
00:30:55,220 --> 00:30:55,830
Come on.

600
00:30:55,980 --> 00:30:56,900
Ma'am...

601
00:30:58,420 --> 00:31:01,080
Why aren't you mad at me at all?

602
00:31:02,400 --> 00:31:06,140
I'll save my anger for next time.

603
00:31:06,470 --> 00:31:09,510
This time, it was just a mistake.

604
00:31:09,530 --> 00:31:11,500
Let's just let it go.

605
00:31:12,680 --> 00:31:13,990
But in the future,

606
00:31:14,610 --> 00:31:18,580
Soh might have days
where he makes mistakes, too.

607
00:31:23,350 --> 00:31:24,700
And when that day comes,

608
00:31:25,410 --> 00:31:28,120
I want you to stay calm

609
00:31:28,310 --> 00:31:29,670
and give Soh a chance,

610
00:31:30,070 --> 00:31:33,060
just like I'm giving you one today.

611
00:31:35,830 --> 00:31:36,440
Yes, ma'am.

612
00:31:43,230 --> 00:31:45,060
Hey, why that long face?

613
00:31:45,660 --> 00:31:46,840
My mom wasn't even scolding you.

614
00:31:47,090 --> 00:31:48,860
It's just not cool, Soh.

615
00:31:49,270 --> 00:31:51,740
Meeting your mom for the first time,

616
00:31:52,130 --> 00:31:53,480
and I already messed things up.

617
00:31:56,370 --> 00:31:58,400
There, there.

618
00:31:58,930 --> 00:32:00,460
If my mom sees you

619
00:32:00,890 --> 00:32:03,000
making that face,
she's going to worry even more.

620
00:32:03,850 --> 00:32:05,330
I'm just feeling down.

621
00:32:09,270 --> 00:32:10,400
Feeling better now?

622
00:32:14,770 --> 00:32:16,970
Well, almost.

623
00:32:16,990 --> 00:32:19,090
It would be better
if I got a kiss on this side, too.

624
00:32:21,730 --> 00:32:22,870
You've hit your limit.

625
00:32:23,280 --> 00:32:25,060
Wait, there's a limit?

626
00:32:25,260 --> 00:32:26,100
Soh...

627
00:32:27,490 --> 00:32:28,650
It's so freaking hot.

628
00:32:29,110 --> 00:32:29,960
Is it hot, P'Laem?

629
00:32:29,980 --> 00:32:31,250
Yeah, but first of all...

630
00:32:31,280 --> 00:32:33,570
- Six seven!
- Six seven!

631
00:32:38,940 --> 00:32:40,140
Here, take this.

632
00:32:40,150 --> 00:32:42,130
- Don't forget to share.
- Share with each other.

633
00:32:42,500 --> 00:32:44,300
- This is delicious.
- Here it is.

634
00:32:44,320 --> 00:32:45,650
- Don't forget to share.
- Share...

635
00:32:45,660 --> 00:32:46,900
There's only one pack,
and you want them to share?

636
00:32:46,910 --> 00:32:48,920
- Share with you, too.
- Oh, with me? Okay.

637
00:32:49,200 --> 00:32:51,080
- You guys in the back, come!
- Come on!

638
00:32:51,100 --> 00:32:52,460
- Want a book?
- Here you go.

639
00:32:52,750 --> 00:32:54,550
- No one is taking my stuff.
- Yeah.

640
00:32:54,580 --> 00:32:57,120
I've got plenty. Here, want some?

641
00:32:57,540 --> 00:32:58,380
Here, here.

642
00:32:58,700 --> 00:33:00,380
This is super yummy.

643
00:33:00,590 --> 00:33:02,110
Share it, and don't forget

644
00:33:02,120 --> 00:33:03,509
- to save some for me.
- This one is amazing.

645
00:33:03,510 --> 00:33:04,880
Bon appétit.

646
00:33:05,020 --> 00:33:07,650
- Delicious! What did you say?
- Oh, bon appétit.

647
00:33:07,840 --> 00:33:09,740
- Thank you.
- Don't forget!

648
00:33:10,030 --> 00:33:10,800
Books, anyone?

649
00:33:10,820 --> 00:33:12,200
- And this too.
- Hey!

650
00:33:12,930 --> 00:33:14,780
Is Chiang Mai really this small?

651
00:33:15,430 --> 00:33:17,420
How many mountains could there be
in Chiang Mai anyway?

652
00:33:18,110 --> 00:33:19,340
Hey, hey, hey!

653
00:33:19,630 --> 00:33:21,440
Wait a second.

654
00:33:23,160 --> 00:33:23,740
Look.

655
00:33:24,180 --> 00:33:27,140
Hey, kid, where did you find this?

656
00:33:27,420 --> 00:33:28,290
Where did you get this from?

657
00:33:28,320 --> 00:33:30,600
Can I buy it from you? How much?

658
00:33:31,440 --> 00:33:34,190
How about you guys play a match for us?

659
00:33:34,390 --> 00:33:36,020
Bangkok is so far away.

660
00:33:36,040 --> 00:33:38,620
I really want to see you guys compete
with my own eyes.

661
00:33:42,060 --> 00:33:43,020
Calm down.

662
00:33:43,050 --> 00:33:45,970
You really want to see us
play against those guys?

663
00:33:46,010 --> 00:33:50,680
I'll give this keychain to the winner,

664
00:33:51,030 --> 00:33:54,920
so can you guys play a match for me?

665
00:33:55,060 --> 00:33:56,680
Oh, sure.

666
00:33:56,700 --> 00:33:58,620
But you'd better keep your word.

667
00:33:58,790 --> 00:33:59,910
Hey, wait.

668
00:34:00,040 --> 00:34:01,880
Who told you we were going to play?

669
00:34:02,120 --> 00:34:05,000
So, what does "Blue Viper" mean exactly?

670
00:34:05,080 --> 00:34:07,480
A snake that ran out of venom?

671
00:34:07,560 --> 00:34:09,410
If you're this much of a chicken,

672
00:34:09,430 --> 00:34:11,040
why not just change your name
to "Wimp Viper"?

673
00:34:11,060 --> 00:34:13,120
- Wimp Viper sounds better, right?
- Yeah, it suits them.

674
00:34:13,760 --> 00:34:15,840
Forget it. Fine, we'll play.

675
00:34:15,940 --> 00:34:19,040
But you guys have to change your name
to "Big Mouth Brothers," too.

676
00:34:19,060 --> 00:34:21,020
- Big Mouth?
- No problem.

677
00:34:22,140 --> 00:34:23,040
You big-mouth posers.

678
00:34:24,230 --> 00:34:26,050
Why do we have to play RoV against them?

679
00:34:26,570 --> 00:34:28,110
They'll end up
knowing all our strategies.

680
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:32,240
And who said
we're going to play a normal match?

681
00:34:42,510 --> 00:34:44,000
The game we're about to play
is called...

682
00:34:44,380 --> 00:34:46,230
Celestial Clash: Dark Tea Leaves.

683
00:34:46,970 --> 00:34:49,020
(Celestial Clash: Dark Tea Leaves)

684
00:34:49,540 --> 00:34:52,360
The rules are: those three rows
of the tea plantation...

685
00:34:52,700 --> 00:34:54,290
will represent Top Lane,
Mid Lane, and Bottom Lane.

686
00:34:54,350 --> 00:34:56,240
Each team will have their own basket.

687
00:34:56,440 --> 00:34:58,370
Whichever team fills their basket first

688
00:34:58,400 --> 00:35:00,670
will be considered
to have destroyed the enemy tower.

689
00:35:00,890 --> 00:35:02,660
Did I expect way too much from you?

690
00:35:03,340 --> 00:35:04,260
But you're about to find out...

691
00:35:04,300 --> 00:35:07,180
exactly how powerful
Blue Viper really is.

692
00:35:07,220 --> 00:35:09,320
Oh, since you're talking so much trash,

693
00:35:09,340 --> 00:35:11,460
it means
you're already prepared to lose.

694
00:35:12,350 --> 00:35:14,560
- Prepared to lose?
- In that case...

695
00:35:15,040 --> 00:35:15,840
Let the game begin!

696
00:35:15,860 --> 00:35:17,800
- Hey, that's f*cking cheating!
- Bring it on!

697
00:35:27,680 --> 00:35:30,410
We'd better not lose this, damn it.
Go, Blue Viper!

698
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:35,400
Let's go, team! Fill the basket.

699
00:35:36,250 --> 00:35:37,200
Right here.

700
00:35:38,330 --> 00:35:39,370
Keep going.

701
00:35:40,340 --> 00:35:41,890
You can do it, P'Three!

702
00:35:41,920 --> 00:35:42,900
Keep it up!

703
00:35:46,120 --> 00:35:46,830
Go, go!

704
00:35:48,160 --> 00:35:49,240
Let's do this, guys!

705
00:35:49,870 --> 00:35:51,100
B.S. Brothers!

706
00:35:51,170 --> 00:35:54,120
Pluck all this, take the championship!

707
00:35:54,140 --> 00:35:55,770
Are you here for the trophy
or just for fun?

708
00:35:55,920 --> 00:35:59,080
Whoa, I didn't know there were chickens
on this mountain!

709
00:35:59,610 --> 00:36:00,950
Cock-a-doodle-doo!

710
00:36:00,970 --> 00:36:02,680
You are the chickens.

711
00:36:02,710 --> 00:36:03,870
I'm gonna peck your eyes out.

712
00:36:03,900 --> 00:36:06,520
Hey, let's focus on quality,
not just speed.

713
00:36:06,550 --> 00:36:08,380
- Yeah, and forget those Vipers.
- Alright.

714
00:36:08,410 --> 00:36:09,800
Focus on quality. Let's go!

715
00:36:09,840 --> 00:36:10,450
You got it.

716
00:36:10,970 --> 00:36:13,040
- Buy Fenrir's Tooth. Get an attack speed item.
- Get me Fenrir's Tooth.

717
00:36:13,060 --> 00:36:16,040
Get the Blade of Eternity.
You won't die. Keep going.

718
00:36:16,070 --> 00:36:17,320
- Alright, deal.
- Move fast!

719
00:36:17,340 --> 00:36:18,150
Hey, Soh!

720
00:36:18,170 --> 00:36:19,200
Put it in!

721
00:36:19,700 --> 00:36:20,960
We need to invade their jungle.

722
00:36:21,750 --> 00:36:22,460
You in?

723
00:36:22,490 --> 00:36:24,040
Let's go. If you're in, I'm in.

724
00:36:25,720 --> 00:36:26,310
Keep going!

725
00:36:26,340 --> 00:36:27,960
Soh, heal me.

726
00:36:28,020 --> 00:36:28,710
You got this!

727
00:36:28,790 --> 00:36:30,530
Now I'm motivated. Let's go!

728
00:36:30,560 --> 00:36:32,680
- P'Three!
- Why are you picking a leaf?

729
00:36:32,820 --> 00:36:33,730
You're supposed to pick tea leaves.

730
00:36:33,760 --> 00:36:34,800
Yeah, pick the tea leaves.

731
00:36:34,820 --> 00:36:37,040
If you can't do that,
you'd better go home and cry.

732
00:36:37,550 --> 00:36:38,820
Whoa!

733
00:36:38,850 --> 00:36:39,890
You're about to find out.

734
00:36:40,130 --> 00:36:42,040
You'll see. It's called teamwork.

735
00:36:45,020 --> 00:36:47,000
Hey! Can I pick this one like this?

736
00:36:47,030 --> 00:36:48,600
- Quick! Faster!
- Let's go!

737
00:36:48,660 --> 00:36:49,280
Got it.

738
00:36:49,500 --> 00:36:51,280
Soh! This one, here!

739
00:36:53,540 --> 00:36:54,720
This is the prime tea tip!

740
00:37:03,450 --> 00:37:04,400
Hey, you okay?

741
00:37:04,420 --> 00:37:05,670
- I'm fine!
- You sure?

742
00:37:05,700 --> 00:37:06,540
Ow, ow!

743
00:37:06,610 --> 00:37:07,560
That's my hair!

744
00:37:07,680 --> 00:37:08,920
My bad, my bad.

745
00:37:08,940 --> 00:37:10,000
- My bad, bro.
- My hair's a mess now.

746
00:37:14,150 --> 00:37:15,780
He must be feeling left out,

747
00:37:16,160 --> 00:37:17,600
having to stand there like an extra.

748
00:37:26,530 --> 00:37:28,240
Whoa, Preaw, are you okay?

749
00:37:29,330 --> 00:37:30,560
I think I twisted my ankle.

750
00:37:30,580 --> 00:37:32,120
How about you get some rest?

751
00:37:32,140 --> 00:37:34,250
It's okay. You stay here.
I'll go by myself.

752
00:37:35,950 --> 00:37:38,000
Wait, aren't you going to play?

753
00:37:38,070 --> 00:37:39,380
Go take her place.

754
00:37:41,970 --> 00:37:43,040
I'm not on that team.

755
00:37:43,330 --> 00:37:46,680
Oh, really? But I've seen you guys
compete on the same team.

756
00:37:48,290 --> 00:37:49,540
Yeah, Number.

757
00:37:50,240 --> 00:37:53,040
Your name, Three, is a number.

758
00:37:53,190 --> 00:37:55,130
Ten is a number, too.

759
00:37:55,510 --> 00:37:56,860
My name sits right next to a number,

760
00:37:57,040 --> 00:37:58,240
meaning I'm right beside you two.

761
00:38:14,670 --> 00:38:16,690
Go rest. I'll sub in for you.

762
00:38:17,010 --> 00:38:18,680
Aren't you with Blue Viper?

763
00:38:18,910 --> 00:38:20,410
How can you play for us?

764
00:38:21,400 --> 00:38:22,260
Why not?

765
00:38:22,510 --> 00:38:25,640
If the RoV league finds out
I switched teams for a tea-picking game,

766
00:38:26,190 --> 00:38:27,280
am I going to get banned?

767
00:38:29,260 --> 00:38:29,930
Go.

768
00:38:32,020 --> 00:38:33,680
Look, tea tips!

769
00:38:34,150 --> 00:38:35,650
- Here, here!
- Soh...

770
00:38:35,670 --> 00:38:37,080
- Put them in!
- I'm here to help.

771
00:38:37,110 --> 00:38:38,430
Yeah, great.

772
00:38:39,390 --> 00:38:41,070
What kind of joke are you playing at?

773
00:38:41,200 --> 00:38:42,580
If it's a joke, then laugh.

774
00:38:42,750 --> 00:38:43,960
Why the serious face?

775
00:38:45,400 --> 00:38:47,970
I don't have time to argue with you.
I'm serious.

776
00:38:48,490 --> 00:38:50,840
Aren't you afraid your teammates
will say you betrayed them?

777
00:38:51,590 --> 00:38:52,640
Screw them.

778
00:38:53,040 --> 00:38:54,280
They're going to trash-talk me anyway.

779
00:38:54,850 --> 00:38:56,970
What exactly are you trying to do?

780
00:38:57,160 --> 00:38:58,590
You've been abandoning me all this time.

781
00:38:58,670 --> 00:39:00,330
And now what?
Did you just realize...

782
00:39:01,010 --> 00:39:02,750
what it's like to be abandoned?

783
00:39:12,360 --> 00:39:13,170
Yeah.

784
00:39:13,600 --> 00:39:15,920
I'm back to help now.
What more do you want?

785
00:39:16,380 --> 00:39:17,720
Don't you think it's a little too late?

786
00:39:18,990 --> 00:39:19,760
P'Three...

787
00:39:25,390 --> 00:39:26,880
If you actually want to help me,

788
00:39:27,090 --> 00:39:28,440
don't make us lose.

789
00:39:30,090 --> 00:39:31,360
Just try to keep up with me.

790
00:39:34,710 --> 00:39:35,560
What the hell?

791
00:39:35,850 --> 00:39:37,120
What's your problem?

792
00:39:37,140 --> 00:39:38,280
- What's wrong with you?
- Why?

793
00:39:38,310 --> 00:39:39,760
What's your deal?

794
00:39:40,020 --> 00:39:41,880
- Why? What's up with you?
- Come on! Bring it on!

795
00:39:45,150 --> 00:39:46,010
Soh, come here.

796
00:40:08,240 --> 00:40:11,320
Blue Viper has more tea leaves.

797
00:40:13,050 --> 00:40:14,440
Bring it!

798
00:40:15,390 --> 00:40:16,640
Easy!

799
00:40:17,720 --> 00:40:20,250
It's fine, Mr. Three.
You might lose this time, but...

800
00:40:20,940 --> 00:40:23,760
- you're gonna lose in the APL anyway.
- Exactly.

801
00:40:24,780 --> 00:40:27,940
- Hey, let's go sip some tea.
- Let's go!

802
00:40:27,970 --> 00:40:29,360
Wait a second.

803
00:40:30,300 --> 00:40:32,500
We only count the young tea leaves.

804
00:40:32,580 --> 00:40:34,860
The mature ones don't count.

805
00:40:35,460 --> 00:40:38,720
Based on the results,

806
00:40:38,760 --> 00:40:42,430
B.S. Brothers is the winner!

807
00:40:44,140 --> 00:40:45,020
What the hell?

808
00:40:45,040 --> 00:40:46,280
- What now?
- What?

809
00:40:46,300 --> 00:40:49,720
- Here we go! Wimp Viper!
- Wimp Viper! Wimp Viper!

810
00:40:49,750 --> 00:40:52,040
- One more time! Wimp Viper!
- Wimp Viper!

811
00:40:52,770 --> 00:40:54,610
You don't have to change the name
to Wimp Viper, though.

812
00:40:54,630 --> 00:40:56,940
We were just teasing, you know.

813
00:40:56,970 --> 00:40:59,790
- Come on, Wimp Viper!
- Wimp Viper!

814
00:41:00,910 --> 00:41:03,360
- It smells so good.
- Truly refreshing.

815
00:41:06,200 --> 00:41:07,400
Hey, kid...

816
00:41:07,420 --> 00:41:08,360
Wait!

817
00:41:09,880 --> 00:41:10,440
Hey...

818
00:41:11,980 --> 00:41:12,770
Where is it?

819
00:41:13,030 --> 00:41:15,910
Where's the thing you promised?
Don't forget.

820
00:41:18,460 --> 00:41:19,440
Here you go.

821
00:41:20,580 --> 00:41:22,800
Usually, I sell these
for thirty baht each,

822
00:41:22,830 --> 00:41:25,230
but I'll give this to you for free.

823
00:41:26,810 --> 00:41:27,770
For free?

824
00:41:29,520 --> 00:41:30,830
Thirty baht?

825
00:41:36,510 --> 00:41:38,480
Why did you rush over here?

826
00:41:38,500 --> 00:41:39,080
Oh...

827
00:41:40,910 --> 00:41:41,980
Here, ma'am.

828
00:41:42,120 --> 00:41:43,640
I bought this for you.

829
00:41:44,770 --> 00:41:46,300
I'm truly sorry.

830
00:41:46,740 --> 00:41:50,460
Although this can't replace
your actual anniversary gift,

831
00:41:50,760 --> 00:41:52,960
I still wanted to give it to you.

832
00:41:55,470 --> 00:41:58,660
Actually, Soh bought it for me.

833
00:42:01,410 --> 00:42:05,360
And it wasn't
an anniversary gift at all.

834
00:42:08,760 --> 00:42:10,420
I'm sorry to you, too.

835
00:42:10,810 --> 00:42:13,400
You look exhausted.

836
00:42:17,910 --> 00:42:21,740
She's definitely
the most difficult boss to win.

837
00:42:30,440 --> 00:42:34,130
Thank you, son.

838
00:42:35,430 --> 00:42:38,780
I saw how much effort you put in.

839
00:42:42,860 --> 00:42:47,390
Even if it really were
my wedding anniversary gift,

840
00:42:48,130 --> 00:42:49,920
I wouldn't have minded.

841
00:42:50,220 --> 00:42:52,130
Things can be lost,

842
00:42:52,710 --> 00:42:55,750
but this precious son of mine...

843
00:42:56,350 --> 00:42:57,680
can't be.

844
00:43:03,720 --> 00:43:04,940
Don't you worry, Mom.

845
00:43:05,060 --> 00:43:06,910
While regular jobs might have days off,

846
00:43:08,950 --> 00:43:11,700
taking care of Soh is a job
I'll never take a break from

847
00:43:12,130 --> 00:43:13,310
because I'm doing it from the heart.

848
00:43:22,670 --> 00:43:24,860
Don't expect
any overtime pay from me, though.

849
00:43:30,460 --> 00:43:32,410
Thank you so much, son.

850
00:43:40,930 --> 00:43:41,710
No problem.

851
00:43:57,550 --> 00:43:58,720
This sucks.

852
00:44:01,210 --> 00:44:02,600
Hey, Ten.

853
00:44:04,370 --> 00:44:05,140
Sorry, man.

854
00:44:05,740 --> 00:44:07,040
All seats are taken.

855
00:44:07,990 --> 00:44:09,250
Why don't you head back
with your old friends?

856
00:44:11,750 --> 00:44:13,130
Oh, I forgot.
He doesn't have any friends.

857
00:44:14,410 --> 00:44:15,840
A guy with no friends, huh?

858
00:44:18,770 --> 00:44:20,050
Hey, we're just kidding.

859
00:44:22,900 --> 00:44:24,820
I've got a spare seat for you.

860
00:44:40,250 --> 00:44:41,300
Want to ride in our truck?

861
00:44:43,280 --> 00:44:45,090
There's still some room for you.

862
00:44:46,240 --> 00:44:47,200
If you want to come, you can.

863
00:44:55,490 --> 00:44:57,220
You don't need to
swing back for me anymore.

864
00:44:59,480 --> 00:45:01,170
I'm done heading
in the same direction as you guys.

865
00:45:04,360 --> 00:45:05,970
What exactly do you mean by that?

866
00:45:06,100 --> 00:45:08,000
You know exactly what I mean.

867
00:45:11,660 --> 00:45:12,310
Dammit!

868
00:45:38,970 --> 00:45:41,680
I'm not going to thank you for the ride.

869
00:45:42,750 --> 00:45:44,030
Let's just call it even

870
00:45:44,770 --> 00:45:45,870
since I helped you out, too.

871
00:45:47,310 --> 00:45:48,020
Yeah.

872
00:45:48,970 --> 00:45:51,220
See you in the next match, then.

873
00:45:52,360 --> 00:45:53,790
If you're still with Blue Viper,
that is.

874
00:45:57,430 --> 00:45:59,320
If I'm still with Blue Viper,

875
00:45:59,720 --> 00:46:00,840
you won't stand a chance.

876
00:46:17,740 --> 00:46:18,440
Ten...

877
00:46:21,640 --> 00:46:22,130
Wait.

878
00:46:23,680 --> 00:46:25,260
Aren't you heading back
with B.S. Brothers?

879
00:46:26,350 --> 00:46:28,680
I don't feel very comfortable
sleeping at Soh's mom's place.

880
00:46:32,140 --> 00:46:32,830
So what?

881
00:46:35,490 --> 00:46:37,040
Want to stay the night with me?

882
00:46:39,470 --> 00:46:42,380
Can't I just piggyback off you
and stay at a luxury hotel for once?

883
00:46:45,450 --> 00:46:46,900
Just tell me what's really on your mind.

884
00:46:49,450 --> 00:46:51,060
Well, the tournament is over now.

885
00:46:54,220 --> 00:46:55,730
I'm just here to keep my promise.

886
00:47:16,760 --> 00:47:18,500
So, what are you going to do next?

887
00:47:19,110 --> 00:47:20,840
Are you going back to Blue Viper?

888
00:47:24,030 --> 00:47:24,950
Probably not.

889
00:47:26,490 --> 00:47:27,860
I want to take a break for a bit,

890
00:47:29,110 --> 00:47:30,890
and then I'll find a place
where I actually belong.

891
00:47:32,550 --> 00:47:34,210
Then just stay right here with me.

892
00:47:38,730 --> 00:47:40,060
Don't you remember...

893
00:47:40,360 --> 00:47:43,720
that a Jack card always belongs
right next to a Ten?

894
00:47:45,360 --> 00:47:46,780
That's so cringe.

895
00:47:46,890 --> 00:47:47,620
Come on.

896
00:47:50,610 --> 00:47:54,170
I'm glad you and Three
are actually talking again

897
00:47:55,170 --> 00:47:57,140
even if it's not on the best of terms.

898
00:47:58,250 --> 00:47:59,420
But honestly,

899
00:48:00,250 --> 00:48:01,730
back when we were all still friends,

900
00:48:02,060 --> 00:48:04,410
we weren't exactly nice
to each other, either.

901
00:48:07,350 --> 00:48:08,150
True.

902
00:48:10,310 --> 00:48:11,650
But come to think of it,

903
00:48:12,640 --> 00:48:14,640
you're kind of like a boxing referee.

904
00:48:15,400 --> 00:48:17,570
Whenever Three and I got into it,

905
00:48:18,260 --> 00:48:19,580
you always stayed neutral,

906
00:48:20,590 --> 00:48:22,010
never taking sides.

907
00:48:25,830 --> 00:48:27,740
I guess I was just being selfish,

908
00:48:28,350 --> 00:48:30,100
wanting you to be on my side,

909
00:48:31,470 --> 00:48:35,920
even when I was clearly
the one in the wrong.

910
00:48:39,420 --> 00:48:41,090
I really hated it, man,

911
00:48:42,750 --> 00:48:44,960
whenever you chose Three over me.

912
00:48:50,250 --> 00:48:51,800
I want you to know...

913
00:48:52,330 --> 00:48:55,460
that I never stopped choosing you.

914
00:49:01,690 --> 00:49:04,810
When I started
distancing myself from you,

915
00:49:05,370 --> 00:49:07,300
it wasn't because
I chose to be on his side.

916
00:49:07,870 --> 00:49:09,740
I was going through some personal sh*t,

917
00:49:10,870 --> 00:49:13,160
and I knew that if you found out,

918
00:49:13,560 --> 00:49:15,980
you'd dive right in to help me
with everything you had.

919
00:49:19,270 --> 00:49:21,160
I just didn't want
to feel pathetic, man,

920
00:49:22,960 --> 00:49:26,020
having to let you fix my problems
over and over again.

921
00:49:33,430 --> 00:49:34,450
And you know what?

922
00:49:36,170 --> 00:49:37,710
I f*cking hated it...

923
00:49:39,120 --> 00:49:41,090
when I was left all alone.

924
00:49:46,630 --> 00:49:47,980
- We did it!
- Number one!

925
00:49:48,010 --> 00:49:49,180
(I'm super excited right now,)

926
00:49:49,200 --> 00:49:50,870
(and I'm really, really happy)

927
00:49:50,890 --> 00:49:53,500
(that everyone voted for us
to be the MVPs.)

928
00:49:53,980 --> 00:49:56,140
(Alright, thank you to all the fans)

929
00:49:56,160 --> 00:49:57,370
(who voted for us...)

930
00:49:57,400 --> 00:49:59,280
(Because I don't want to play
with you guys anymore!)

931
00:50:01,410 --> 00:50:02,390
(Goddammit!)

932
00:50:06,760 --> 00:50:08,420
I just felt like you and Three

933
00:50:09,660 --> 00:50:11,440
were slowly drifting away from me.

934
00:50:19,740 --> 00:50:21,260
Further and further away...

935
00:50:23,060 --> 00:50:25,440
until the distance between us
grew huge.

936
00:50:27,360 --> 00:50:29,950
So huge that sometimes
I felt like I was all alone.

937
00:50:38,450 --> 00:50:40,020
I screwed everyone over.

938
00:50:40,990 --> 00:50:41,990
I did you dirty.

939
00:50:43,160 --> 00:50:44,300
I did Three dirty.

940
00:50:46,830 --> 00:50:48,180
I just felt so much pain

941
00:50:50,190 --> 00:50:53,200
because I thought my wounds
were the deepest in the world...

942
00:50:55,220 --> 00:50:56,820
to the point where I started thinking

943
00:50:58,310 --> 00:50:59,540
that maybe it was okay...

944
00:51:02,670 --> 00:51:05,150
to hurt others just to protect myself.

945
00:51:09,010 --> 00:51:11,870
That's why I chose
to betray you and everyone.

946
00:51:28,420 --> 00:51:29,410
I'm sorry...

947
00:51:30,290 --> 00:51:32,520
if I ever made you feel that way.

948
00:51:36,230 --> 00:51:37,700
I should apologize to everyone.

949
00:51:38,900 --> 00:51:39,920
And you...

950
00:51:46,480 --> 00:51:48,480
Can I come back to you now?

951
00:51:55,450 --> 00:51:57,420
I told you I'd be by your side,

952
00:51:58,890 --> 00:52:00,300
and I will stay...

953
00:52:02,370 --> 00:52:04,780
even on the days
when you're not on your own side.

954
00:52:05,590 --> 00:52:06,560
Remember that.

955
00:53:13,010 --> 00:53:15,860
We should bring
P'Toobtub and P'Jane next time.

956
00:53:15,920 --> 00:53:17,900
Exactly. If P'Toobtub were here,

957
00:53:17,950 --> 00:53:19,520
we wouldn't have to pay for the booze.

958
00:53:20,140 --> 00:53:22,640
And he could've helped
carry these suitcases, too.

959
00:53:22,660 --> 00:53:25,600
- So heavy. No idea what's in here.
- Yeah.

960
00:53:25,700 --> 00:53:27,480
Wait, where's Jack?

961
00:53:27,880 --> 00:53:29,620
I haven't seen him since last night.

962
00:53:29,640 --> 00:53:30,700
P'Jack?

963
00:53:30,810 --> 00:53:33,560
I called him last night.
He said he'd catch up with us.

964
00:53:34,400 --> 00:53:36,500
I've got his suitcase right here.
It's heavy as f*ck.

965
00:53:36,530 --> 00:53:37,250
I know.

966
00:53:37,670 --> 00:53:38,800
What the hell did he pack?

967
00:53:40,530 --> 00:53:41,800
Speak of the devil. There he is.

968
00:53:41,850 --> 00:53:42,370
Hey!

969
00:53:46,300 --> 00:53:47,940
- Whoa!
- Hey, hi!

970
00:53:49,110 --> 00:53:50,440
Alright, okay.

971
00:53:50,500 --> 00:53:53,140
- Goodbye. Thank you for having us.
- Goodbye.

972
00:53:54,070 --> 00:53:55,640
- We're heading off now. Goodbye.
- Goodbye!

973
00:53:55,760 --> 00:53:56,560
Let's go, Soh.

974
00:53:56,920 --> 00:53:57,780
P'Three...

975
00:53:59,410 --> 00:54:01,100
Let's stay in Chiang Mai a bit longer.

976
00:54:01,680 --> 00:54:02,860
Just the two of us.

977
00:54:08,620 --> 00:54:10,140
I've already rescheduled our flights.

978
00:54:10,930 --> 00:54:13,810
Wow, someone's going to have a blast.

979
00:54:14,390 --> 00:54:15,820
Have a great trip, you two,

980
00:54:15,970 --> 00:54:18,020
now that you won't have
any third wheels like us.

981
00:54:18,050 --> 00:54:20,050
Oh, wait! We haven't even
been to Tha Phae yet.

982
00:54:20,080 --> 00:54:22,480
- I've got an idea.
- Whoa, wait! No.

983
00:54:22,500 --> 00:54:24,500
- Just go home.
- Guess I'll just head back, then.

984
00:54:24,530 --> 00:54:25,270
Yeah.

985
00:54:25,300 --> 00:54:27,310
- You want to get rid of me that badly?
- No, I love being with you.

986
00:54:27,340 --> 00:54:29,790
- Go. Just get out of here.
- Alright. We're off. See ya!

987
00:54:29,820 --> 00:54:30,410
See ya.

988
00:54:30,930 --> 00:54:32,390
Goodbye!

989
00:54:35,260 --> 00:54:36,400
I seriously can't believe him.

990
00:54:39,410 --> 00:54:41,640
Well, enjoy your trip.

991
00:54:42,370 --> 00:54:43,270
Thanks, Mom.

992
00:54:43,490 --> 00:54:44,580
Goodbye.

993
00:54:45,010 --> 00:54:46,520
Come here, give me a hug.

994
00:54:49,930 --> 00:54:52,100
- We're off. Goodbye and thank you.
- Bye-bye.

995
00:54:55,380 --> 00:54:57,140
So, what should we do now?

996
00:54:57,810 --> 00:54:58,960
Wanna go to the zoo?

997
00:54:59,850 --> 00:55:01,400
How about coming to see
a capybara in my room?

998
00:55:02,990 --> 00:55:06,150
♪Love isn't a game we play,♪

999
00:55:06,200 --> 00:55:08,380
♪You can't just start again another day♪

1000
00:55:08,410 --> 00:55:11,910
Where are you taking me today, Derya?

1001
00:55:12,500 --> 00:55:15,640
Anywhere is fine
as long as I'm with you.

1002
00:55:16,150 --> 00:55:17,200
You're so sweet.

1003
00:55:17,210 --> 00:55:18,800
Give me a kiss. Come on.

1004
00:55:18,810 --> 00:55:19,870
Hurry up.

1005
00:55:20,140 --> 00:55:23,220
♪You're the only one in my heart♪

1006
00:55:23,390 --> 00:55:25,420
- Kiss...
- Give me a kiss.

1007
00:55:28,480 --> 00:55:30,880
Soh, I think something's wrong
with the sticky rice.

1008
00:55:30,910 --> 00:55:32,040
It sticks to everything.

1009
00:55:33,510 --> 00:55:35,860
Just like how I'm stuck on you.

1010
00:55:36,920 --> 00:55:38,940
It's not sticking to my hands at all.

1011
00:55:43,190 --> 00:55:45,620
Oops, it's sticking to your lips, too.

1012
00:55:48,050 --> 00:55:50,360
♪By doing this every single day♪

1013
00:55:50,390 --> 00:55:52,360
♪Even if you never look my way♪

1014
00:55:52,380 --> 00:55:54,520
♪(You never look my way)♪

1015
00:55:55,800 --> 00:55:58,470
This is what a romantic trip
should be like.

1016
00:55:59,390 --> 00:56:01,470
We haven't finished
the full experience yet, though.

1017
00:56:02,540 --> 00:56:03,780
Look at these fangs...

1018
00:56:04,080 --> 00:56:05,800
Fang-tas-tic...

1019
00:56:10,120 --> 00:56:12,810
- Do I look fang-tas-tic?
- Absolutely.

1020
00:56:16,290 --> 00:56:19,920
- Do I really look fang-tas-tic?
- Yes, really.

1021
00:56:31,350 --> 00:56:34,370
Thank you for not giving up, P'Three.

1022
00:56:35,820 --> 00:56:37,280
As long as I have you by my side,

1023
00:56:37,570 --> 00:56:39,930
I'll never give up on anything.

1024
00:56:42,030 --> 00:56:44,210
I'll always be here to support you.

1025
00:56:45,110 --> 00:56:46,970
I won't let your HP drop.

1026
00:56:47,940 --> 00:56:50,870
You're being cute again.

1027
00:56:55,390 --> 00:56:59,410
♪I'll find my way
into your heart one day,♪

1028
00:56:59,460 --> 00:57:02,770
♪Getting a little closer every day,♪

1029
00:57:02,790 --> 00:57:06,190
♪Before you even look my way,♪

1030
00:57:08,470 --> 00:57:12,400
♪Before you realize I'm here to stay♪

1031
00:57:12,850 --> 00:57:16,880
♪For now,
I'll just keep things brotherly♪

1032
00:57:16,910 --> 00:57:19,970
♪While caring for you secretly♪

1033
00:57:19,990 --> 00:57:23,970
♪I'll leave no signs for you to see♪

1034
00:57:25,330 --> 00:57:32,360
♪Until your heart makes room for me♪

1035
00:59:49,150 --> 00:59:53,330
♪The answer is you whenever I ask my heart,♪

1036
00:59:53,560 --> 00:59:57,840
♪Can't get over you though I try so hard♪

1037
00:59:57,980 --> 01:00:02,800
♪I'm afraid that love could pull us apart♪

1038
01:00:02,820 --> 01:00:06,840
♪If I'm the only one who's loving with all my heart♪

1039
01:00:06,980 --> 01:00:10,720
♪So many times I've rehearsed the line♪

1040
01:00:11,000 --> 01:00:15,360
♪To tell you that I wish you were mine,♪

1041
01:00:15,400 --> 01:00:24,280
♪But I turn into a coward every time
you look in my eyes♪

1042
01:00:24,310 --> 01:00:29,310
♪Maybe the risk is too high to take,♪

1043
01:00:29,340 --> 01:00:33,680
♪Just being near you is enough for my sake,♪

1044
01:00:33,700 --> 01:00:42,200
♪But my heart beats so fast that I can't fake♪

1045
01:00:42,380 --> 01:00:46,390
♪I'll find my way into your heart one day,♪

1046
01:00:46,450 --> 01:00:49,710
♪Getting a little closer every day,♪

1047
01:00:49,740 --> 01:00:53,200
♪Before you even look my way,♪

1048
01:00:55,470 --> 01:00:59,400
♪Before you realize I'm here to stay♪

1049
01:00:59,830 --> 01:01:03,890
♪For now, I'll just keep things brotherly♪

1050
01:01:03,910 --> 01:01:06,960
♪While caring for you secretly♪

1051
01:01:06,980 --> 01:01:11,080
♪I'll leave no signs for you to see♪

1052
01:01:12,420 --> 01:01:19,400
♪Until your heart makes room for me♪
